1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:03,294
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:13,638
<i>From now on, I'll be the one</i>
<i>to talk to Ivy.</i>

3
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:18,977
<i>It's time to find out if that woman</i>
<i>is with us or against us.</i>

4
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:22,814
[Ivy] <i>Señor Julio has returned</i>
<i>to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

5
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,149
<i>We have to be more careful.</i>

6
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:26,860
<i>I'll speed up my search</i>
<i>for my mother, Jepoy.</i>

7
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:30,238
<i>You wouldn't try</i>
<i>to poison me again, would you?</i>

8
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:32,657
<i>Anyone who opposes me will be punished.</i>

9
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:35,285
<i>And you, Emilia, I'll make you suffer.</i>

10
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:39,122
<i>You'll see just how cruel</i>
<i>your father can be.</i>

11
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,541
<i>Grandpa wants to meet with her tomorrow.</i>

12
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:44,919
<i>Please tell her to be careful</i>
<i>and not to go with them.</i>

13
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:47,839
<i>You should give me the money</i>
<i>you promised me.</i>

14
00:00:47,922 --> 00:00:49,174
<i>We should join forces.</i>

15
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:51,968
<i>With your wealth and my influence.</i>

16
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,553
[Ivy] <i>The election's still far off.</i>

17
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:55,847
<i>Now's not the time.</i>

18
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,641
[Emilia]<i> Raul, I'm sure Papa</i>
<i>will have you killed.</i>

19
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,518
<i>You better stay at your parents' place</i>

20
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:01,978
<i>in San Ildefonso.</i>

21
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,897
[Ivy]<i> San Ildefonso.</i>

22
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:07,067
<i>That's where Raul</i>
<i>could be hiding my mother.</i>

23
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:09,778
<i>I have a suspicion that Miss Aguas</i>

24
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,029
<i>is hiding something.</i>

25
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:12,363
<i>I want you to follow her.</i>

26
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:17,952
[Arnaldo] <i>It's important that</i>
<i>I can trust my staff, Madrigal.</i>

27
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:20,747
<i>If not, you might end up dead.</i>

28
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,917
[Clarita] <i>You aren't alone in</i>
<i>your fight against your father.</i>

29
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,836
<i>We will bring him down by whatever means!</i>

30
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,297
<i>The Torillo's residence?</i>
<i>Go straight ahead.</i>

31
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:32,091
<i>You'll find an old lone house there.</i>

32
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,010
<i>Is something wrong, Diego?</i>

33
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:35,762
<i>Do you remember what I told you</i>
<i>last night?</i>

34
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:39,682
<i>Don't worry. I won't leave</i>
<i>until she comes back.</i>

35
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:42,977
[tense music playing]

36
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:48,858
Diego, what's that?

37
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:53,780
Miss Carlotta, who's this?

38
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:57,242
That's Miss Prianka, Miss Ivy's mother.

39
00:01:57,325 --> 00:01:59,452
No, not her. The girl. Who is she?

40
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:02,789
I don't know.

41
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:06,417
She's probably one of the kids
who used to visit us.

42
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:10,380
But Ivy told me that she was always alone.

43
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:13,842
Well, sometimes we'd get
visitors, of course.

44
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:17,387
Like the children
of Miss Prianka's friends.

45
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:22,517
Give me that, Diego.

46
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,895
Ivy doesn't like people
looking through her things.

47
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:29,149
Here.

48
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:32,318
Finish your drink before you leave.

49
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:34,863
Ivy called and said
that she might take a while.

50
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:37,532
Miss Carlotta, I don't mean to be rude…

51
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:42,412
but is Ivy Miss Prianka Aguas'
real daughter?

52
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:45,665
-Of course--
-I found information

53
00:02:45,748 --> 00:02:46,791
on the Internet

54
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:49,752
that says Prianka Aguas'
daughter is Angel Aguas.

55
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,172
Is she Ivy's sister?

56
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:57,844
And why don't Prianka and Ivy look alike?

57
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,596
I mean, their features--

58
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,848
Ivy took after her father.

59
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:05,184
And yes, Ivy had a sister. But she's dead.

60
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:11,149
Good grief, Diego.
Stop with the questions.

61
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:15,111
I think it's better if you leave now.

62
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,031
I'm so sorry, Miss Carlotta.

63
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:23,244
Well then, I'll be off.

64
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:24,495
All right.

65
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:29,792
[tense music playing]

66
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:48,519
Diego's catching on to Ivy.

67
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:53,066
He can't be.

68
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:57,028
He just can't.

69
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,497
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

70
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,123
<i>Please try again later.</i>

71
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:10,959
[clicks tongue]

72
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:12,794
Oh, Ivy…

73
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:22,679
Moving back here has done
you good, Congressman.

74
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:25,682
It seems like you're recovering very fast.

75
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,976
The love from my family

76
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:31,521
and the townspeople does wonders, Doc.

77
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:33,856
Oh, by the way.

78
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:36,276
I'd like to ask a favor from you.

79
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:41,781
Can you tell
the other politicians you know,

80
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:43,950
well, and your patients too…

81
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:48,705
that Julio Ardiente is back
in town and he's very much okay?

82
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:51,582
No problem, Congressman. I'll do that.

83
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:54,502
-Okay.
-Thank you very much, Doc.

84
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:56,879
Take your medication.
Remember, health is wealth.

85
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:57,964
Yes.

86
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:01,968
Doc.

87
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:04,095
Oh.

88
00:05:04,595 --> 00:05:05,805
-Grandpa.
-[grunts]

89
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:11,728
Where did Miss Aguas go?

90
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:15,898
We weren't able to find her, Grandpa.

91
00:05:17,608 --> 00:05:20,945
So, in other words, she got away.

92
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:24,615
[tense music playing]

93
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:28,786
Maybe she knew you were following her?

94
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:34,083
Oh, well. It doesn't matter.

95
00:05:35,793 --> 00:05:39,922
I'm just wondering where
Miss Aguas could have gone.

96
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:44,886
Has she gone to Manila…

97
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:51,100
or maybe to my political rivals
in other provinces?

98
00:05:53,936 --> 00:05:56,606
Maybe she and Raul are in cahoots…

99
00:05:57,774 --> 00:05:58,941
along with Emilia.

100
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:02,820
They might be planning
something against me.

101
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:08,367
Or against <i>us</i>.

102
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:14,123
[Julio exhales]

103
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:16,292
You know, Arnaldo…

104
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:20,671
I'm losing faith in that woman.

105
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,840
[tense music playing]

106
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:30,223
What do you want me to do, Grandpa?

107
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:55,915
Excuse me, sir.

108
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,084
Yes, ma'am?

109
00:06:58,167 --> 00:07:00,378
I'm sorry, but may I ask you something?

110
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:01,546
-What is it?
-Do you know

111
00:07:01,629 --> 00:07:02,880
where the Torillo house is?

112
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:05,216
Yes. It's in the middle of that forest.

113
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:07,760
Um…

114
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:10,763
Is it still far from here?
Do you think I can drive there?

115
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:13,891
I don't think so, ma'am.
You better leave it here.

116
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,351
-Can I?
-Yes.

117
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:18,104
-Can I park my car here?
-Sure.

118
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:20,606
Just park it at the back of my house.

119
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:21,774
Thank you, sir.

120
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:23,192
-Sure. No problem.
-Thank you.

121
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:29,240
[pensive music playing]

122
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:45,381
-Thanks again, sir.
-No problem, ma'am.

123
00:07:50,052 --> 00:07:54,265
[pensive music playing]

124
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:06,569
[tense music playing]

125
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:20,833
[groans]

126
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:41,896
[whimpers]

127
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,195
[sobbing]

128
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:53,866
Mom, are you here?

129
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:04,335
[sobbing]

130
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:16,472
[screaming]

131
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:17,723
[dishes break]

132
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:20,184
[suspenseful music playing]

133
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:26,607
Mom?

134
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:33,698
Mom?

135
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:35,491
[groans]

136
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:36,951
[whimpering]

137
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:39,537
Mom?!

138
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:43,583
Mom!

139
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:48,754
Mom!

140
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,464
[wailing]

141
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:52,800
Mom!

142
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:08,107
Mom!

143
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:12,194
[tense music swelling]

144
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:13,904
[crying]

145
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:30,379
Mom!

146
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:36,177
Mom?

147
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:38,721
Mom?

148
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:40,473
Mom!

149
00:10:44,977 --> 00:10:45,853
[grunts]

150
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:46,854
Mom!

151
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:52,318
[grunting]

152
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,038
Mom?

153
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:10,586
[instrumental theme music playing]

154
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,181
Mom?

155
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:30,648
Mom?

156
00:11:31,649 --> 00:11:36,362
[instrumental theme music playing]

157
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:39,657
Mom?

158
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:52,420
Mom?

159
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:11,439
Mom…

160
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,984
[gasping]

161
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:21,657
It's you!

162
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:25,411
Mom!

163
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:43,471
-Mom. Mom!
<i>-♪ Let her cry ♪</i>

164
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:46,807
<i>♪ For she's a lady ♪</i>

165
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:54,899
<i>♪ Let her dream, for she's a child ♪</i>

166
00:12:54,982 --> 00:13:01,697
<i>♪ Let the rain fall down upon her ♪</i>

167
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,866
-Mom!
<i>-♪ She's a free and gentle ♪</i>

168
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:09,497
-My mom! It's really you!
<i>-♪ Flower growing wild ♪</i>

169
00:13:10,539 --> 00:13:14,460
<i>♪ And if by chance that</i>
<i>I should hold her ♪</i>

170
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:17,796
<i>♪ Let me hold her for a time ♪</i>

171
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,758
<i>♪ But if allowed just one possession ♪</i>

172
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:21,800
[Ivy weeping] Mom…

173
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:26,680
<i>♪ I would pick her from</i>
<i>The garden to be mine ♪</i>

174
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,265
You're alive!

175
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:31,644
I thought you were dead, but you're alive!

176
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,437
Mom.

177
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:36,857
Mom…

178
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:38,776
[screaming]

179
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:39,902
Mom?

180
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:41,695
Mom?

181
00:13:42,613 --> 00:13:44,532
Mom? [shushes] Mom?

182
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,951
<i>♪ Be careful how you touch her ♪</i>

183
00:13:47,034 --> 00:13:48,035
Mom.

184
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:52,373
Mom.

185
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:56,460
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda
continues playing]

186
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,257
Mom, it's me.

187
00:14:05,135 --> 00:14:06,845
It's me, your daughter.

188
00:14:10,391 --> 00:14:12,476
Don't you recognize me, Mom?

189
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,855
Mom, it's me, Lily.

190
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:25,531
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda
continues playing]

191
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:27,408
Lily?

192
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:28,993
Mom.

193
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:32,413
Yes, Mom, it's me.

194
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:33,914
It's me, Lily.

195
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:36,709
I am Lily!

196
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:41,964
I'm Lily, Mom.

197
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,139
Mom, I'm Lily.

198
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:53,225
It's me, Lily. Please believe me.

199
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:59,857
It's me, Mom.

200
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:03,736
Here, look.

201
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:05,571
[battery dies]

202
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:17,875
[solemn instrumental playing]

203
00:15:22,504 --> 00:15:23,505
Mom!

204
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:25,674
Look at me.

205
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:27,468
It's me.

206
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:30,387
Mom, I'm Lily.

207
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:36,602
Mom.

208
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:41,607
Mom, it's me, Lily.

209
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:44,401
Lily Cruz.

210
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:46,195
My name's Lily Cruz.

211
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:50,115
My father is Dante Cruz.

212
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:54,161
[stutters] He was a public attorney, Mom.

213
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,915
And you were a teacher.

214
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,043
Uh…

215
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:06,882
We moved to Poblacion Ardiente
because Dad was assigned there.

216
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:08,884
But…

217
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:13,180
But the Ardientes killed him.

218
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:19,019
And I thought they killed you too.

219
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,480
I thought you were dead.

220
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:27,111
Mom, it's me, your Lily.

221
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:33,117
Mom, I'm your daughter.

222
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,203
Your only daughter.

223
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:38,580
Mom…

224
00:16:38,872 --> 00:16:40,374
[suspenseful music]

225
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:42,626
[Dante] <i>Attorney Dante Cruz.</i>

226
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:44,420
<i>This is my daughter, Lily,</i>
<i>and wife, Camia.</i>

227
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:46,839
<i>We'll have the peaceful life</i>
<i>you've been dreaming of.</i>

228
00:16:46,922 --> 00:16:48,424
[Camia] <i>Dante?! Dante!</i>

229
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,175
[whimpering]

230
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:51,885
Mom, what's happening?

231
00:16:52,386 --> 00:16:54,722
Mom, what's happening?

232
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:56,223
[screaming]

233
00:16:56,306 --> 00:16:58,058
-Mom!
-[Camia screaming]

234
00:16:58,142 --> 00:16:59,143
Mom, wait!

235
00:16:59,476 --> 00:17:00,477
Mom!

236
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:02,271
Mom!

237
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:04,481
Mom, wait!

238
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:06,817
Mom? Mom!

239
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:08,402
Mom, hold on.

240
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:12,281
-[Camia grunting]
-Mom?! It's me, Lily!

241
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:13,449
Mom!

242
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:15,826
[Lily knocking on door] Mom!

243
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:17,453
Mom!

244
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,747
Mom, open the door.

245
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:23,042
-[Camia wailing]
-Mom, aren't you happy?

246
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:26,587
Aren't you happy to see me again?

247
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:29,590
Mom!

248
00:17:30,257 --> 00:17:31,425
Mom?!

249
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,762
[Camia wailing]

250
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:37,473
Mom.

251
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:52,571
You're my mother.

252
00:17:55,991 --> 00:17:58,702
It's me, Lily. I'm your daughter.

253
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,084
Please believe me.

254
00:18:07,002 --> 00:18:09,505
I'm your daughter, Lily.

255
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,008
Mom.

256
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:14,885
Mom.

257
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:19,139
Mom.

258
00:18:20,724 --> 00:18:22,810
[crying]

259
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:25,604
[screaming]

260
00:18:25,687 --> 00:18:26,647
Mom!

261
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:30,734
Mom!

262
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,323
Mom. Mom.

263
00:18:39,326 --> 00:18:40,410
Mom.

264
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:42,621
Mom, what's going on?

265
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:49,711
Can't you remember me?

266
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:51,463
Or anything?

267
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:00,848
Mom.

268
00:19:01,515 --> 00:19:02,724
[sniffles]

269
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,482
What did they do to you, Mom?

270
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,320
What did they do to you?

271
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,823
What happened to you?

272
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:21,410
What did they do to you, Mom?

273
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:26,874
[tense music playing]

274
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,343
[car door opens]

275
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,764
[car door closes]

276
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:47,686
Let's get out of here.

277
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:53,066
We have to, Mom. Please come with me.

278
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:10,250
I'll take you home.

279
00:20:18,091 --> 00:20:19,885
[grunts, clears throat]

280
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:32,397
[suspenseful music playing]

281
00:20:52,876 --> 00:20:53,835
Love?

282
00:20:58,882 --> 00:20:59,883
Love?!

283
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:02,302
What happened, Love?! Why?

284
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:04,429
Hey…

285
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:07,015
What happened, Love?!
Why are you crying again?

286
00:21:07,432 --> 00:21:08,725
What happened?!

287
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,478
Does anything hurt?! Tell me! What?

288
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:13,772
Don't cry. I'm here now.

289
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:17,025
I won't leave you again.
I'm here now, Jasmin.

290
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:21,697
[tense music playing]

291
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:43,969
[groans]

292
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:46,888
What is it?

293
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:50,767
Listen to me, love.

294
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,185
What's the problem?

295
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:54,896
What is it? Is there
something you want to tell me?

296
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,356
Go ahead. I'm listening.

297
00:21:57,065 --> 00:21:58,066
Go on.

298
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:03,780
Tell me.

299
00:22:07,284 --> 00:22:08,327
What is it?

300
00:22:09,619 --> 00:22:10,746
Tell me.

301
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:37,981
[tense music continues playing]

302
00:22:52,746 --> 00:22:53,789
Come.

303
00:22:54,331 --> 00:22:56,333
Come with me.

304
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:58,710
You might need something to eat.

305
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:00,253
You might be hungry. Come on.

306
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:20,899
[tense music continues playing]

307
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:37,916
Raul, you bastard.

308
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:49,845
Ivy, answer the phone.

309
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,974
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

310
00:23:54,057 --> 00:23:55,851
Ivy, where are you?

311
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:59,020
Where are you?

312
00:23:59,229 --> 00:24:00,564
[phone ringing]

313
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:02,315
-Hello, Jepoy?
-Nanny.

314
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:04,526
Jepoy, thank goodness you called!

315
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:06,069
Are you with Ivy?

316
00:24:06,278 --> 00:24:08,155
You mean she hasn't come home yet?

317
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:10,323
She hasn't. I've been trying to call her,

318
00:24:10,407 --> 00:24:11,867
but I can't reach her.

319
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:14,452
<i>Oh, Jepoy!</i>

320
00:24:14,536 --> 00:24:16,830
What if something bad happened to Ivy?!

321
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:18,582
[exhales]

322
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:22,460
Uh, don't worry. I'll look for her.

323
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:24,921
Okay. Please do, Jepoy!

324
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:27,257
And keep me updated, okay?

325
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:29,968
-Be careful.
-I will.

326
00:24:39,144 --> 00:24:40,145
Madrigal.

327
00:24:42,856 --> 00:24:44,024
[tense music playing]

328
00:24:44,107 --> 00:24:45,650
Where are you going?

329
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:48,195
To town, Mayor. For a few drinks.

330
00:24:48,278 --> 00:24:51,031
[tense music playing]

331
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:52,866
I need you to be here early tomorrow.

332
00:24:52,949 --> 00:24:53,992
Don't be late.

333
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,203
Yes, Mayor.

334
00:24:57,996 --> 00:24:58,997
I'll go on ahead.

335
00:24:59,581 --> 00:25:00,665
All right.

336
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:19,809
[pensive music playing]

337
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:26,441
<i>I'm sure of it.</i>

338
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:28,652
<i>That girl is Lily.</i>

339
00:25:30,320 --> 00:25:31,905
<i>I need to know the truth.</i>

340
00:25:33,448 --> 00:25:35,033
<i>If they don't want to tell me,</i>

341
00:25:35,700 --> 00:25:37,160
<i>then I'll look into it myself.</i>

342
00:25:41,331 --> 00:25:45,335
[pensive music continues playing]

343
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:40,223
[scoffs]

344
00:26:41,933 --> 00:26:43,184
Emilia.

345
00:26:45,145 --> 00:26:46,438
Emilia.

346
00:27:18,053 --> 00:27:19,137
[exhales]

347
00:27:27,645 --> 00:27:29,522
You pathetic woman.

348
00:27:41,951 --> 00:27:43,828
Look at what you did, love.

349
00:27:44,412 --> 00:27:47,207
You destroyed our doorknob
because you wanted to go out.

350
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:50,460
You know you can't, right?
It's dangerous out there.

351
00:27:50,919 --> 00:27:55,090
Don't worry, I'm not mad.
Just don't do it again, okay?

352
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:56,299
Come here.

353
00:27:58,134 --> 00:28:02,263
Did you know I prepared dinner for you?

354
00:28:03,181 --> 00:28:04,724
I'm sure you'll love it.

355
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:07,685
Auntie Belen said this
is your favorite dish.

356
00:28:07,769 --> 00:28:10,730
She says whenever she cooks this for you,

357
00:28:10,814 --> 00:28:12,399
you always end up eating a lot.

358
00:28:12,732 --> 00:28:16,152
And I'm sure you'll eat a lot of this…

359
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:19,823
because Auntie Belen
didn't make this, I did.

360
00:28:20,323 --> 00:28:21,574
Here.

361
00:28:21,658 --> 00:28:23,076
I cooked this.

362
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:26,830
I'll join you. Wait right there.

363
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:33,169
You know, love?

364
00:28:34,212 --> 00:28:38,925
I know you're uncomfortable here
because this place is dark.

365
00:28:40,176 --> 00:28:44,389
So I want to apologize…

366
00:28:45,682 --> 00:28:48,518
if it's dark and hard to move around.

367
00:28:49,102 --> 00:28:51,521
<i>Why is he calling Mom "love"?</i>

368
00:28:51,604 --> 00:28:54,274
<i>He even called her "Jasmin".</i>

369
00:28:54,607 --> 00:28:57,610
We're only using gas lamps
but look at it, love.

370
00:28:58,653 --> 00:29:01,114
It's romantic, like we're on a date.

371
00:29:02,115 --> 00:29:05,076
And, love, I'll fix those stairs.

372
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,077
I have to close it off.

373
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:08,580
It's too dangerous for you to go upstairs.

374
00:29:08,663 --> 00:29:10,707
You should stay downstairs, okay?

375
00:29:11,875 --> 00:29:12,959
Let's eat.

376
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:22,343
I'm excited for you to try this because--

377
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:24,137
[phone ringing]

378
00:29:25,180 --> 00:29:26,306
Hold on.

379
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:28,558
[phone ringing]

380
00:29:33,313 --> 00:29:34,397
Hold on, love.

381
00:29:34,481 --> 00:29:36,649
[phone continues ringing]

382
00:29:44,032 --> 00:29:45,033
Hello?

383
00:29:46,075 --> 00:29:49,162
Good thing you answered my call.

384
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:51,748
What do you need from me, Papa?

385
00:29:54,959 --> 00:29:55,960
[chuckles lightly]

386
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:57,337
"Papa"?

387
00:29:58,254 --> 00:30:00,673
<i>You still have the nerve to call me Papa…</i>

388
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:04,302
after what you did?!

389
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:07,263
Can you please stop
beating around the bush?

390
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:09,140
What is it?

391
00:30:09,224 --> 00:30:11,267
Tell it to me straight.
What do you want from me?

392
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:13,478
You're tough now, huh, Raul?

393
00:30:14,103 --> 00:30:15,104
<i>Well then…</i>

394
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:17,565
Come here.

395
00:30:18,149 --> 00:30:20,568
Come back to the mansion.

396
00:30:21,110 --> 00:30:26,074
And stop hiding
under your mistress' skirt.

397
00:30:26,366 --> 00:30:27,116
[scoffs]

398
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:30,703
<i>What? Cat got your tongue?</i>

399
00:30:31,454 --> 00:30:34,624
Or maybe you want my men to come get you?

400
00:30:35,333 --> 00:30:36,334
<i>Well, Raul?</i>

401
00:30:37,001 --> 00:30:39,546
<i>Choose. What do you want?</i>

402
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:44,092
Hey! Leave your pit and face me.

403
00:30:45,176 --> 00:30:48,137
<i>Stop hiding like a cowardly rat.</i>

404
00:30:48,221 --> 00:30:49,931
Face me, you coward!

405
00:30:50,890 --> 00:30:53,184
If you want me to go there,
then fine, I will.

406
00:30:53,268 --> 00:30:55,645
But I'm not a coward
because I'm not afraid of you.

407
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:03,862
[laughing]

408
00:31:03,945 --> 00:31:06,364
[sighs deeply]

409
00:31:08,157 --> 00:31:11,327
[pensive music playing]

410
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:19,919
[clears throat]

411
00:31:23,214 --> 00:31:26,885
I'm sorry about that.
That was an important call.

412
00:31:30,597 --> 00:31:33,099
<i>He might take Mom with him.</i>

413
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:35,143
<i>I can't let that happen.</i>

414
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:40,398
<i>I need to find a way</i>
<i>to get Mom out of here.</i>

415
00:31:45,528 --> 00:31:46,446
Guess what, Pa.

416
00:31:46,529 --> 00:31:51,367
The people at the office
are very happy that you're back.

417
00:31:52,952 --> 00:31:55,830
I'm glad to hear someone is.

418
00:31:57,290 --> 00:31:59,500
What about you, Emilia? Are you happy?

419
00:32:00,001 --> 00:32:01,085
Of course, Papa. I'm--

420
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:04,964
-Julio!
-Don't lie to me!

421
00:32:08,551 --> 00:32:09,802
But it's okay.

422
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:14,015
Tonight, all your lies
will come to an end.

423
00:32:14,974 --> 00:32:17,810
You and your husband's lies will end here.

424
00:32:17,894 --> 00:32:20,063
Do you know Raul is on his way here now?

425
00:32:21,356 --> 00:32:23,566
And Arnaldo will finally know the truth.

426
00:32:26,486 --> 00:32:27,695
What do you mean, Grandpa?

427
00:32:29,405 --> 00:32:31,366
Papa, don't do this.

428
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:33,159
Don't destroy our family.

429
00:32:34,243 --> 00:32:35,870
I'm not ruining it.

430
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:40,667
On the contrary,
I am strengthening this family.

431
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:44,045
Because I want us to live together

432
00:32:44,128 --> 00:32:47,757
without hiding any secrets
from each other.

433
00:32:49,258 --> 00:32:50,259
[scoffs]

434
00:32:51,094 --> 00:32:52,136
You know, Arnaldo?

435
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:55,848
What you'll learn will surprise you.

436
00:32:56,099 --> 00:32:58,601
And I'm sure it will change

437
00:32:58,685 --> 00:33:00,770
how you see both your Mom and your Dad.

438
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:07,735
Well, I don't want to wait
for Dad anymore, Grandpa.

439
00:33:08,861 --> 00:33:10,279
I want to know now.

440
00:33:15,159 --> 00:33:16,202
Uh…

441
00:33:18,079 --> 00:33:19,330
[dramatic music]

442
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:31,676
[thudding]

443
00:33:33,594 --> 00:33:36,889
Love, I'm closing this off.

444
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:39,308
So you can't go upstairs.

445
00:33:40,143 --> 00:33:41,144
Come.

446
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:48,693
Love…

447
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:53,573
I'm sorry, but I really have to leave now.

448
00:33:55,366 --> 00:33:57,410
I want all this to end.

449
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:02,832
I'm doing this for us, for our peace.

450
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:07,253
Remember, Jasmin, I love you very much.

451
00:34:08,129 --> 00:34:09,380
You are my life.

452
00:34:11,466 --> 00:34:13,885
Don't worry about where I'm going.

453
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:16,971
They won't hurt me.

454
00:34:17,638 --> 00:34:19,724
They owe a lot to my father.

455
00:34:20,767 --> 00:34:23,102
And I know plenty of secrets about them.

456
00:34:23,186 --> 00:34:24,854
This will all end tonight.

457
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:28,316
I promise to come back to you right away.

458
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:30,485
Okay?

459
00:34:38,409 --> 00:34:41,204
You should get some sleep.

460
00:34:41,871 --> 00:34:42,997
Come on.

461
00:34:43,623 --> 00:34:48,002
[tense music playing]

462
00:34:53,633 --> 00:34:54,634
[keys jingle]

463
00:35:04,727 --> 00:35:07,855
[tense music swelling]

464
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:19,659
I'll be back first thing tomorrow.

465
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:02,368
[car unlocks]

466
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:15,965
<i>Mayor, we'll take the other road.</i>

467
00:36:16,048 --> 00:36:17,425
<i>There's an intersection at the end.</i>

468
00:36:17,508 --> 00:36:18,759
<i>We can catch her there.</i>

469
00:36:27,226 --> 00:36:29,187
Ivy… Where are you?

470
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:34,066
Have you found your mother?

471
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:45,870
[groans]

472
00:37:19,111 --> 00:37:20,279
Mom, please stand up.

473
00:37:20,696 --> 00:37:22,907
We'll get out of here, okay?

474
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:25,159
Come here. We have to leave
before he comes back.

475
00:37:25,243 --> 00:37:27,245
-Hurry, Mom.
-I don't want to.

476
00:37:35,753 --> 00:37:36,671
Raul!

477
00:37:36,754 --> 00:37:39,131
Didn't I tell you not to come here?

478
00:37:39,215 --> 00:37:40,508
Where's that father of yours?

479
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,468
-Raul, wait!
-Hold on.

480
00:37:42,551 --> 00:37:43,594
Raul!

481
00:37:43,678 --> 00:37:45,721
Raul! Stop it!

482
00:37:45,805 --> 00:37:47,265
I just want to talk to your father.

483
00:37:47,974 --> 00:37:49,058
Raul!

484
00:37:50,226 --> 00:37:51,269
Raul.

485
00:37:57,024 --> 00:37:58,776
My, my.

486
00:38:00,027 --> 00:38:03,197
I didn't expect you to come here, Raul.

487
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:06,826
I thought you'd run with your tail

488
00:38:06,909 --> 00:38:10,830
between your legs and cower
under your women's skirts.

489
00:38:11,038 --> 00:38:13,416
-Let's get this over with, Papa.
-Not so fast!

490
00:38:14,041 --> 00:38:15,084
Back off!

491
00:38:16,335 --> 00:38:17,712
What do you think you're doing?!

492
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:19,213
What now?

493
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:21,382
Do it! Come closer!

494
00:38:22,383 --> 00:38:24,510
I won't let you hurt Grandpa again!

495
00:38:26,387 --> 00:38:28,139
I know everything. They told me.

496
00:38:28,931 --> 00:38:31,892
I know what you traitors did!

497
00:38:33,019 --> 00:38:34,186
How could you do that?!

498
00:38:34,687 --> 00:38:36,522
And why did you cover it up?!

499
00:38:38,357 --> 00:38:41,152
My own parents? You ingrates!

500
00:38:41,694 --> 00:38:43,362
Hold on, Arnaldo…

501
00:38:43,863 --> 00:38:46,532
Do you know whom you're
pointing your gun at?!

502
00:38:47,033 --> 00:38:48,993
-I'm your father!
-He's my grandfather!

503
00:38:51,662 --> 00:38:53,497
If you think I'm the devil in the flesh…

504
00:38:54,290 --> 00:38:55,708
then what about your grandfather?

505
00:38:56,834 --> 00:38:58,794
He's worse than the devil himself!

506
00:39:00,254 --> 00:39:03,758
I just want to tell you
that what I did to him

507
00:39:03,883 --> 00:39:08,512
was nothing compared
to what he's done to me!

508
00:39:11,098 --> 00:39:14,727
If there's something
I regret not doing, Arnaldo,

509
00:39:14,810 --> 00:39:16,479
that's not killing him!

510
00:39:16,562 --> 00:39:18,773
I should've killed that
worthless grandfather of yours!

511
00:39:19,690 --> 00:39:22,860
How dare you say that in front of me!

512
00:39:24,820 --> 00:39:27,031
You worthless bastard!

513
00:39:27,490 --> 00:39:29,367
Are you really testing me?!

514
00:39:29,450 --> 00:39:32,203
Why, what'll you do?! Tell me!

515
00:39:32,495 --> 00:39:33,662
Why don't you pull the trigger?!

516
00:39:34,914 --> 00:39:36,082
Do it!

517
00:39:41,962 --> 00:39:43,464
Mom, listen to me.

518
00:39:43,547 --> 00:39:46,967
We have to leave
before that bastard returns.

519
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:48,969
I'll set you free, Mom.
We'll escape together.

520
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:50,971
Let's go. Hurry up.

521
00:39:51,347 --> 00:39:53,140
Let's go, Mom.

522
00:39:53,307 --> 00:39:55,768
-No. No!
-Mom. Mom!

523
00:39:56,602 --> 00:39:57,853
I'll stay here.

524
00:39:59,688 --> 00:40:00,815
You're staying here?

525
00:40:02,316 --> 00:40:04,735
Mom, what did that man do to you?

526
00:40:07,488 --> 00:40:09,949
Mom, did he abuse you?

527
00:40:10,032 --> 00:40:12,910
Did he make you drink something
that made you forget who I am?

528
00:40:13,744 --> 00:40:16,747
Mom, do you know what that man did to you?

529
00:40:17,373 --> 00:40:20,251
He once tried to rape you.

530
00:40:21,085 --> 00:40:26,382
Then, his wife ordered Dad,
you, and me to be killed!

531
00:40:26,465 --> 00:40:27,466
All of us, Mom!

532
00:40:28,050 --> 00:40:30,219
He's a bad person! So is his family!

533
00:40:30,302 --> 00:40:32,263
-We should leave.
-No!

534
00:40:33,055 --> 00:40:35,391
-He's kind. He's kind.
-Come on, Mom…

535
00:40:36,142 --> 00:40:37,268
Who's "kind"?!

536
00:40:38,769 --> 00:40:39,812
That man?

537
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:42,857
You think that bastard is kind?!

538
00:40:43,941 --> 00:40:45,609
He isn't "kind"!

539
00:40:46,277 --> 00:40:49,488
He isn't because he's the reason
why we became like this!

540
00:40:49,572 --> 00:40:53,117
Why we fell apart!
Why our family has become like this!

541
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:54,577
He isn't kind!

542
00:40:58,706 --> 00:41:00,124
Not even close!

543
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:08,466
[Jepoy] I couldn't find Ivy…

544
00:41:09,675 --> 00:41:11,594
What if something happened to her?

545
00:41:12,219 --> 00:41:13,679
Let's not jump to conclusions.

546
00:41:14,972 --> 00:41:15,890
Ivy is always ready.

547
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:19,143
Whatever happens, she can defend herself.

548
00:41:19,393 --> 00:41:21,562
But what if she's already found Camia?

549
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:25,065
And now Raul has both of them?

550
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:28,944
I'll see what I can do.

551
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:33,574
If something that big happens,
the Ardientes will know.

552
00:41:33,949 --> 00:41:36,785
Be careful. Stay away from here for now.

553
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:39,872
Call or text me any information you have.

554
00:41:40,539 --> 00:41:42,750
-I will.
-Thank you.

555
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:45,628
Where could she be?

556
00:41:47,796 --> 00:41:48,714
-That's enough!
-What--

557
00:41:48,797 --> 00:41:52,134
Stop it! Stop it, all of you!
That's enough!

558
00:41:53,427 --> 00:41:55,095
Don't do this, Papa.

559
00:41:55,846 --> 00:41:57,431
Please forgive us.

560
00:41:58,098 --> 00:41:59,642
We're sorry, Papa.

561
00:42:03,521 --> 00:42:06,190
I will never forgive you.

562
00:42:07,525 --> 00:42:09,443
You ruined everything.

563
00:42:10,277 --> 00:42:11,529
Especially you, Emilia!

564
00:42:13,113 --> 00:42:17,326
You let ambition and power eat you up.

565
00:42:20,829 --> 00:42:25,125
You've tainted this family's name.

566
00:42:25,501 --> 00:42:29,838
And worst of all,
you killed my good friend.

567
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:32,508
You killed Pablo!

568
00:42:32,591 --> 00:42:33,509
[grunts]

569
00:42:33,592 --> 00:42:35,010
Enough of that already!

570
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:39,223
You're hurting Emilia! This isn't right!

571
00:42:39,390 --> 00:42:42,768
I say what's wrong
and right in this house.

572
00:42:42,935 --> 00:42:45,312
And you, don't try to play a hero.

573
00:42:45,396 --> 00:42:46,939
Step aside. Move!

574
00:42:47,022 --> 00:42:49,692
That's enough, Papa! Please…

575
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:51,777
Stop it, please.

576
00:42:51,944 --> 00:42:53,279
You listen, Emilia!

577
00:42:54,655 --> 00:42:56,407
Everything about you…

578
00:42:57,032 --> 00:42:59,118
everything, is over.

579
00:43:00,661 --> 00:43:05,457
I'll take away your rights
as a mother, a daughter…

580
00:43:06,208 --> 00:43:08,836
and the right to be an Ardiente.

581
00:43:09,253 --> 00:43:10,421
[gasps]

582
00:43:13,132 --> 00:43:17,011
And from that high cloud
you're sitting on,

583
00:43:17,803 --> 00:43:19,221
you will fall.

584
00:43:21,056 --> 00:43:23,726
You are going to resign

585
00:43:23,809 --> 00:43:26,437
as governor of Poblacion Ardiente.

586
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:30,649
And then people will see you
for who you really are.

587
00:43:31,692 --> 00:43:34,361
A weak, weak woman!

588
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:36,363
[Emilia crying]

589
00:43:42,161 --> 00:43:43,162
Let's go, Mom.

590
00:43:43,829 --> 00:43:46,832
Believe me, Mom. It's me, Lily!

591
00:43:46,915 --> 00:43:49,960
-Come with me--
-Who is Lily?!

592
00:43:50,961 --> 00:43:52,963
Who is Lily?

593
00:43:55,257 --> 00:44:00,929
Mom, I know you know who Lily is.

594
00:44:02,765 --> 00:44:06,226
Maybe your mind can't remember me,

595
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:08,896
but I know your heart does.

596
00:44:10,439 --> 00:44:12,941
You didn't tell Raul about me.

597
00:44:14,318 --> 00:44:17,863
Mom, It's me, Lily.

598
00:44:19,156 --> 00:44:20,824
I'm your daughter, Lily.

599
00:44:21,492 --> 00:44:23,410
-I don't have--
-Come on, Mom.

600
00:44:23,494 --> 00:44:24,912
We have to get out of here. Let's go.

601
00:44:24,995 --> 00:44:26,705
-I don't have a daughter.
-Come on, Mom.

602
00:44:26,789 --> 00:44:30,292
-I don't have a daughter.
-You do. It's me, Lily.

603
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:32,961
No! I don't!

604
00:44:36,173 --> 00:44:39,218
[sobbing]

605
00:44:40,427 --> 00:44:44,348
[instrumental theme music playing]

606
00:45:16,547 --> 00:45:22,761
[instrumental theme music
continues playing]

607
00:45:32,312 --> 00:45:33,647
You can't do this, Papa.

608
00:45:33,730 --> 00:45:35,107
You cannot do this!

609
00:45:35,190 --> 00:45:36,817
That's unconstitutional! I'll sue you!

610
00:45:36,900 --> 00:45:41,280
I will not give you the right
or the chance to say that!

611
00:45:43,532 --> 00:45:45,033
Because I'll make the people believe

612
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:47,703
you have a life-threatening disease.

613
00:45:47,786 --> 00:45:51,248
Don't worry, I'll find
the perfect disease for you.

614
00:45:51,331 --> 00:45:52,249
[Emilia crying]

615
00:45:52,332 --> 00:45:56,170
We'll call for
a press conference tomorrow,

616
00:45:56,253 --> 00:46:00,966
so you can announce
your resignation as governor.

617
00:46:01,049 --> 00:46:02,718
No, no, Papa…

618
00:46:03,218 --> 00:46:07,347
Papa, please. I'm begging you.
Please, Papa.

619
00:46:07,431 --> 00:46:11,143
Don't do this to me.
Take away everything from me.

620
00:46:11,226 --> 00:46:12,853
Just let me stay as governor.

621
00:46:12,936 --> 00:46:14,354
Please, Papa. Please.

622
00:46:14,438 --> 00:46:15,772
You want to keep your governorship?

623
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:16,815
Yes.

624
00:46:16,899 --> 00:46:19,818
That's easy. Here's the solution.

625
00:46:20,402 --> 00:46:24,531
Shoot Raul, and you can continue
being governor.

626
00:46:25,574 --> 00:46:26,909
There's your choice.

627
00:46:26,992 --> 00:46:28,202
Here.

628
00:46:29,119 --> 00:46:32,039
Just kill Raul, and you
can keep your governorship.

629
00:46:33,624 --> 00:46:34,666
[Julio] Well?

630
00:46:38,253 --> 00:46:39,546
[Julio laughs]

631
00:46:39,630 --> 00:46:40,589
So, I see.

632
00:46:41,465 --> 00:46:45,260
You'd rather choose
the life of that imbecile.

633
00:46:45,886 --> 00:46:47,721
Well, that's fine by me.

634
00:46:50,349 --> 00:46:54,603
From now on, none of you
are allowed to leave this house.

635
00:46:55,229 --> 00:46:57,147
We'll show everyone in this town

636
00:46:58,232 --> 00:47:02,110
that we love you
while you battle your sickness.

637
00:47:02,819 --> 00:47:03,904
As for you, Raul,

638
00:47:04,738 --> 00:47:08,116
you'll show everyone that you love Emilia

639
00:47:08,200 --> 00:47:10,786
and you're concerned with her health.

640
00:47:10,869 --> 00:47:12,538
-Is that clear?
-No.

641
00:47:13,163 --> 00:47:17,459
I will leave this house
whenever I want to.

642
00:47:17,543 --> 00:47:22,839
Unless you want me to expose
this family's dirtiest secrets!

643
00:47:22,923 --> 00:47:25,259
-Oh, please. Go ahead.
-Is that so?

644
00:47:25,342 --> 00:47:28,262
Go ahead, Raul. Give me a reason.

645
00:47:28,345 --> 00:47:31,515
Give me one good reason to be rid of you.

646
00:47:32,224 --> 00:47:34,726
And I'm not joking. I will kill you.

647
00:47:37,396 --> 00:47:38,981
Get them out of here!

648
00:47:39,731 --> 00:47:41,400
-Sir, let's go.
-Wait.

649
00:47:41,483 --> 00:47:42,859
-Papa.
-Please come with us, sir.

650
00:47:42,943 --> 00:47:44,778
-Go!
-[Raul] Emilia! Emilia!

651
00:47:44,861 --> 00:47:45,904
-Raul, stop.
-Let go!

652
00:47:45,988 --> 00:47:47,781
-Raul!
-I can't stay here.

653
00:47:47,864 --> 00:47:48,657
[Emilia] Just go with them.

654
00:47:48,740 --> 00:47:50,117
[Raul] Emilia!

655
00:47:50,200 --> 00:47:55,664
[tense music playing]

656
00:48:15,350 --> 00:48:17,728
<i>Carlotta, I know Ivy's</i>
<i>hiding something from me.</i>

657
00:48:17,811 --> 00:48:19,438
<i>And I swear, I'll find out what it is.</i>

658
00:48:19,521 --> 00:48:21,064
<i>What's this interview for?</i>

659
00:48:21,148 --> 00:48:23,442
[Diego] <i>For a magazine feature</i>
<i>on Miss Aguas.</i>

660
00:48:23,525 --> 00:48:24,443
[woman] <i>Ivy?</i>

661
00:48:24,526 --> 00:48:27,779
<i>According to Mrs. Aguas,</i>
<i>Ivy went through a lot.</i>

662
00:48:27,863 --> 00:48:29,281
[Diego] <i>What do you mean, ma'am?</i>

663
00:48:29,364 --> 00:48:32,200
[woman] <i>Something to do with her</i>
<i>childhood and her real mom.</i>

664
00:48:32,284 --> 00:48:34,953
[Camia] <i>Lily! Lily.</i>

665
00:48:35,037 --> 00:48:37,497
<i>Yes, that's me. Do you remember me now?</i>

666
00:48:37,581 --> 00:48:39,499
<i>-Her real mom?</i>
<i>-Yes.</i>

667
00:48:39,583 --> 00:48:41,877
<i>Ivy is Mrs. Aguas' adopted daughter.</i>

668
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:44,129
<i>-Is this Ivy?</i>
<i>-Yes. That's her.</i>

669
00:48:44,212 --> 00:48:46,298
[Diego] <i>Lily, why did you</i>
<i>have to lie to us?</i>

670
00:48:46,381 --> 00:48:48,133
<i>And why did you come back</i>
<i>to Poblacion Ardiente?</i>

671
00:48:48,216 --> 00:48:51,303
[theme music playing]
